{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411957-astral-exalted-joke","id":1411957,"title":"Astral Exalted (joke)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-04T17:35:39-07:00","id":1411957,"title":"Astral Exalted (joke)","content":"<a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/98/Andromeda_Galaxy_%28with_h-alpha%29.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Behold</a>, what do you see?<br /> <br /> A galaxy full of stars?<br /> <br /> Almost.<br /> <br /> What you see is the distant view, the truly distant view, of the Wyld. Tiny motes of chaos energy, each one surrounding several worlds. The Creation of Exalted resides in one of these, along with its Malfeas, Autocthon, and other strange realms. All contained in one tiny sphere of chaos. The sphere is only tiny compared to the whole of course, as far as those residing in it know it is infinite. In its neighboring balls of chaos reside yet more worlds, many with their own pantheon of Incarna, an primordial titans who created them. Many more lay barren, but almost all are blissfully unaware of the wider world.<br /> <br /> All except the Leitans, the unthinkable beings that spawn and devour these words, the Fustrum, who are the servants they made to enforce their will, and the Astral Exalted in their homes within the Stable Spheres.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Who are the Leitans?</b><br /> <br /> Very little is known about the Leitans. They're beings of astronomical size and power. They are born as their fellow Leitans devour worlds, splitting apart from the new, larger creature, and when they die their corpses vomit out countless new worlds to be devoured. They created the Fustrum, a race of servant beings with incalculable power almost equal to their own, to shepard worlds into their maws.<br /> <br /> <b>Who are the Astral Exalted?</b><br /> <br /> The Astral Exalted were created when the Fustrum discovered that there were sentient creatures within the worlds that they were feeding to the Leitans. Some found pity for these pathetic creatures, the incarna, the titans, and if they strained their vision even weaker creatures. They decided that, although it was not their place to judge, they would give, on occasion, a shard of their power to some of these creatures. That way if their lives were truly worth saving, they could fight for them themselves. Thus were born the Astral Exalted.<br /> <br /> They hide from the Leitans and loyalist Fustrum in worlds shrouded by anonymity and powerful essence magic. Some of these worlds several orders of magnitude larger than Creation, containing cities larger than the Blessed Isle itself. From here they strike out, moving from world to world, battling the loyalist Fustrum, or guiding them towards barren worlds to feed their masters. In rare and desperate occasions they even engage the Leitans directly. Their battlefields almost always span multiple worlds and lead to their destruction.<br /> <br /> <b>How do they work?</b><br /> <br /> Astral Exalted are attribute Exalted, although not like Lunars. First pick a Primary, Secondary and Tertiary attribute, from Physical, Social and Mental. Your starting score is 5 in your primary, 3 in your secondary, and 1 in your tertiary. These attributes may be raised with xp. Your starting Essence score is 1, but note that an Essence 1 Astral Exalt is vastly more powerful than the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Example Physical Charms</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Combat</b><br /> <br /> <b>Apocalypse Attack</b>, Physical 1, Essence 1, 5m: The Astral Exalt sweeps a blade, throws a punch, or otherwise makes violence upon a world. All objects and beings on that plane of existence are subject to Uncountable Damage. Mountains crumble into piles of gravel, bodies explode, and cities topple.<br /> <br /> <b>Merciful Blade</b>, Physical 3, Essence 1: The Astral Exalt may spare some from the ultimate destruction of Apocalypse Attack, preventing anything she deigns worthy of survival from the damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Balewind Strike</b>, Physical 2, Essence 2, 1wp: Even the protections of the gods and Exalted can not save from the powers of the Astral Exalted. Any charm that protects against Uncountable Damage fails against Apocalypse attack, a terrible wind following into the cracks of reality for Seven Shadow Evasion, or whipping around the impenetrable defense of Heavenly Guardian Defense. Many pantheons of Incarna have sat aghast as their invincible leader was cut down with a single stroke from the Astral ones.<br /> <br /> <b>Feats of Athletics</b><br /> <br /> <b>True Speed</b>, Physical 1, Essence 1, 3m: The Astral Exalt can move at the speed of thought, and thus as a reflexive action may move to any place on their current plane of existence if there is an open path.<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy of Interdiction</b>, Physical 2, Essence 2, 2m: As a surcharge to True Speed the Astral Exalt now may bypass any barrier to their destination.<br /> <br /> <b>Tectonic Annihilation</b>, Physical 2, Essence 2, 5m 1wp: The Astral Exalt may manipulate planes as a discus thrower manipulates a disk. By grabbing the ground at the edge of a plane, the Astral Exalt may hurl it at another plane in their region of chaos, causing catastrophic damage to both.<br /> <br /> <b>Stellar Hurl</b>, Physical 5, Essence 4 10m: The Astral upgrades their power from Tectonic Annihilation, giving them the ability to throw chaos spheres, several planes of existence at once, through the void.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Example Social Charms</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Song of Life and Death</b>, Social 3, Essence 2: The Exalt sings a song in their current plane, so beautiful and sad that all living creatures hear it, and then die. Their essence flooding to the Astral and fully replenishing their motepool.<br /> <br /> <b>Interplanar Aria</b>, Social 3, Essence 3: This charm enhances the Song of Life and Death, slaying all creatures in their region of chaos, and refilling the Astral's motepool, and the motepool of one ally per additional plane so drained.<br /> <br /> <b>Final Project</b>, Social 3, Essence 1, 5m 1wp: The Astral contacts all beings in the plane with one voice, and commits them to a project. Thereafter all sentient creatures in that world bend every effort towards the completion of this project, abandoning all other rivalries or concerns.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Example Mental Charms</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Perfect Understanding</b>, Mental 1, Essence 1, 1m: The Astral spends a mote and fully understands whatever they see. Any cypher, or language, writing or symbol the Astral perfectly comprehends. Even the strange thoughts of stellar beings.<br /> <br /> <b>Pursuit of Forgotten Lore</b>, Mental 2 Essence 2: This charm upgrades Perfect Understanding, able now to understand things that once were there, but now gone. Knowledge completely forgotten from somebody's mind, writing from a tablet long turned to dust, or even memories of the once living after sifting through the ashes of a destroyed world.<br /> <br /> <b>Preemptive Reaction Technique</b>, Mental 2, Essence 2, 3m: This charm allows the Astral exalt to move so fast, they react before the thing they were reacting to happens. Invoked reflexively after something happens, they may use this charm to re-write the world, revealing that they took action before the triggering event.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wait a minute, there's no rolls here!</b><br /> <br /> The Astral Exalted leave nothing to chance. When they will something, it is incontestable. The sole exception is in dealing with beings on their level or higher, such as the Fustrum. In this case for each action that could conceivably harm the Fustrum, roll the Astral's essence and deal a health level of damage for each success. This is also the only way to harm beings such beings, the meager attacks of lesser Exalted and Primordial Titans are of no effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:36:36-07:00","id":1411958,"title":"","content":"You want <a href=\"https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/images/character_themuppets_gonzo_9c3596c6.jpeg?region=0,0,300,300\" target=\"_blank\">Gonzo</a>? Get. On. My. <i>LEVEL</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T20:05:31-07:00","id":1411992,"title":"","content":"Cut out the Letians, Fustrum, and Astral Exalted and just leave the \u201cCreation isn\u2019t the only Creation\u201d part and this is what I imagine being a prominent genre of fiction in Exalted Modern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T21:30:29-07:00","id":1412388,"title":"","content":"yup, this is part of my headcanon now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T21:39:52-07:00","id":1412390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411957-astral-exalted-joke?p=1412388#post1412388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yup, this is part of my headcanon now</div> </div> </div> </div>*looks down at the hands that have wrought concepts worse than Dreams of the First Age*<br /> <br /> What have I done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T22:14:54-07:00","id":1412393,"title":"","content":"Galactus and all of its brothers and sisters flying through pure chaos/multiverse with it's heralds and anti-heralds and all of the many islands of universes that are various creations and near creation planes of existence, each universe with various differences that could be as drastic as the primordials all died and pulled their version of creation into that creations void leaving everything lifeless and still to creations that solidified without primordials from the oceans of pure chaos and look much like our current universe to ones where the primordials and exalted generated amazing peace accords and never went to war in the first place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T05:41:02-07:00","id":1412416,"title":"","content":"Nice writeup !<br /> <br /> If you liked the Astral Exalted, you will LOVE the upcoming Galactic Exalted. Basically it's an original new setting with the absolutely ground-breaking idea that each cosmos of Creation is one among billions of others ! They were created by a very powerful and ancient race of transcendant beings, the Natiel, who plays with reality as if they were nothing and consume the essence out of them for sustenance. In order to assist them, the Natiel created the Murtsuf, which may might maybe in some circumstances sort of remind you of the gods of Creation, but if you look deep enough into it you'll notice there are significant differences, that I won't spoil here to preserve the surprise. Anyway, the Murtsuf decided to rebel against their masters (one of the few similarities with the gods of Creation) and in order to do so they chose mortals to imbue with their supreme powers : These heroes are called the Galactic Exalted. They are on a whole new power level that you've never seen before, for example most of the Galactic Exalted are able to destroy a cosmos of Creation with ease (the Leitans stand almost no chance to them).<br /> <br /> Anyway you can find the pdf preview, with 8 original gorgeous illustrations, and 2 short introductory stories, right <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T09:17:38-07:00","id":1412442,"title":"","content":"To prank better, you should probably use a link shortener so people don't see that it leads to YouTube.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T09:25:36-07:00","id":1412443,"title":"","content":"I still have much to learn in the way of the Old Pranker jutsu","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T11:51:15-07:00","id":1412458,"title":"","content":"I think that to a large extent what you have written is a perfectly playable addition to the Exalted setting. I understand the point of the joke and I think you nailed some actual difference of tastes here (and maybe of preferred genres).<br /> <br /> In my headcanon, Creation always used to be a part of some larger whole, (an opinion which isn't very heterodoxical between Well of Udr and Yatani's Children). Of course, since this is a joke, you did not intend it to be actually used in an Exalted campaign, but if this bigger universe were made less uniform, maybe more alien, maybe with more &quot;factions&quot;, definitely without the part where every Creation has its own Malfeas, this could be a basis for a valid plot in the end of a very long, very epic campaign.<br /> <br /> Maybe our Circle just discovered that Gaia's quest to find the Shining Answer was really to find out how to save Creation. She learned that by linking all souls of Creation in telepathic unity, the merged entity can become on par with Fustrum and fight back. Since she did not return, it is now the choice of the players either to convince Incarnae, Yozi, and Neverborn, to perform the ritual of unity; or to escape to some another world which will still last for some time. And, say, Ebon Dragon turns his back on them, and indeed flees and now the Circle has to find him in another world.<br /> <br /> Or maybe our Circle was chosen as advocates of Creation in the majestic trial of Astral courts which are to decide whether this world is worth sparing and they gradually unravel the gravity of their mission.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they can possibly save Creation, but only by granting an Astral shard to their archnemesis Infernal-turned-new-Primordial, but the shard has been sealed eons ago and used to create the Loom of Fate, now guarded by Sidereals and Incarnae unconvinced that Leitans exist at all.<br /> <br /> You know, good, exciting stuff.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that the point of such a grandiose cosmology is not always to be directly interacted with, but also to provide plot hooks for more down-to-Creation campaigns, just like the races from bygone ages which seem to proliferate in the 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 09-07-2020, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T12:24:14-07:00","id":1412462,"title":"","content":"It also makes for the perfect way to end a vanilla Exalted chronicle that\u2019s starting to get stale!<sup><i>[<span style=\"color:blue\">citation needed</span>]</i></sup><br /> <br /> \u201cBalewind Strike, everything dies.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T06:55:22-07:00","id":1412712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411957-astral-exalted-joke?p=1412458#post1412458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, good, exciting stuff.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that the point of such a grandiose cosmology is not always to be directly interacted with, but also to provide plot hooks for more down-to-Creation campaigns, just like the races from bygone ages which seem to proliferate in the 3rd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t actually think that this idea is intrinsically bad, but it would be a really bad idea to have in actual canon. Maybe as a \u201cWhat if? Several possibilities for what lies beyond the Wyld\u201d book or something.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun is nothing more than a gnat, and even if all of Incarna, Primordials, third circle demons, Deathlords, Ishvara and Exalted were unified together, standing as one, the most they could hope to contribute to a battle would be to die in order to replenish the motepools of the astral ones. Which basically means as soon as you directly involve this cosmic conflict your badass Exalt is no longer the kind of hero you probably set out for him to be. Which, again, doesn\u2019t mean that\u2019s a bad game to play, but it\u2019s really not Exalted at that point. Being an Exalt isn\u2019t supposed to be about being utterly powerless in the face of forces so grand you can\u2019t even comprehend them, much less affect them.<br /> <br /> Plus I feel like if you fleshed out the cosmic conflict more, all that would do is give more and more encouragement to STs to include it in their games. Which in turn would make thins like Jiara, Vaneha, Chiaroscuro and the like wasted word count. Nobody cares that Vaneha has a 1,000 mile super-palisade wall to keep out the fey while they go conquering their neighbours when the whole world is just about to be obliterated as collateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T14:42:33-07:00","id":1412908,"title":"","content":"Custom Terrestrial Circle Sorcery Spell: Astral-Smasteral<br /> <br /> Nothing beats the Exalted. Not even homebrew super-Exalted. As soon as anything on a powerscale of the Astral Exalted threatens Solar supremacy, this ancient Emerald Circle Sorcery Spell automatically upgrades every Exalt in Creation to Astral Exalted level. The least Dragon-Blooded raises their Essence to 5 (if lower), and learns every Astral Charm that their highest Attribute in each catagory qualifies them for. Lunars are upgraded to Essence 5 (if lower) then add one to their Essence score, max 10, and learn <i>every</i> Astral Charm, even the ones they don't qualify for. Solars are upgraded to Essence 6, then add one potentially taking them to 11, then they learn every Astral Charm and add Solar Mastery effects to Charms they meet the Attribute prerequisites for -- these Mastery effects are custom to each Solar, but should roughly double the effectiveness of each Charm.<br /> <br /> A yet unformulated Solar Sorcery Spell upgrades all Solars wielding Astral Charms so their Charms have full effect on Leitans (Frustrum and similiar beings), and raises all Solar Attributes to be equal to their Essence Score (if lower). This spell can only be learnt and cast by <i>Solars</i>. No exigents, akuma, Lunars with N/A artifacts, Astral Exalted or other second-raters: only THE BEST Exalted can do this. And it has to be a Twilight. Arianna can do it if you need an NPC to do it for you.<br /> <br /> This spell does nothing for the Incarne, Primordials, mortals, etc. Because the Exalted are the best, and the Solars are the very best. Period.<br /> <br /> Abyssals get raised to Goth Essence 11, which is like Essence 11 but only in Graveyards or when wearing black eyeliner. Infernals and Orichalcum Alchemicals get automatically transformed into Solars.<br /> <br /> Whacka whacka!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-10-2020, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T19:01:48-07:00","id":1412943,"title":"","content":"Agh! Now my 400 page setting book for all the Stable Spheres and their factions might as well be shelved! Next thing you know somebody's going to print a book about how the Haltans and Linowans have found a way to surpass Astral-Smastral and spread across the whole galaxy. Then the only thing that will matter is the internal Halta-Linowan politics!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T20:33:37-07:00","id":1412955,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t worry, all the spells in question are powered by blowing up Gem so the <i>important</i> collateral damage is still safe from interference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 09-11-2020, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}